Source: gimlet-eye-toolkit
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gimlet Eye maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>
# The engine is Rust and the command line is TypeScript, so a build needs both
# toolchains. scripts/rehearse-upgrade.sh installs rustup and Node 20 into a
# container to prove that.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc, nodejs (>= 20), npm
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/James-HoneyBadger/GimletEye
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/James-HoneyBadger/GimletEye.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: gimlet
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20)
Recommends: gnupg
Description: local workbench for system, crypto, and metadata tasks
 One tool registry, one report format, one configuration file, one audit trail,
 and one command line for system administration, file encryption and signing,
 and metadata removal, plus the engine it runs those tools in.
 .
 Everything runs locally: no network calls, no telemetry, no auto-update. There
 is no daemon and no listening port.
